<title>USA: General Magic cuts 80 jobs, sees charge.</title>
<headline>General Magic cuts 80 jobs, sees charge.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Magic Inc Monday said it has cut its work force to 200 regular and contract employees from approximately 280, a move which will result in a fourth quarter charge ranging from $2 to $4 million.</p>
<p>&quot;This was not an easy decision,&quot; said Steve Markman, General Magic's president and chief executive officer, &quot;however, we believe the reduction allows us to better focus on opportunities we see ahead, as well as conserve our nearly $80 million in cash.&quot;</p>
<p>General Magic provides Internet software for business professionals, developers, device manufacturers, service providers and enterprises.</p>
